feature: split-leaderboard-boxes
description: |
  Split the full /leaderboard route into two independent projections: a
  System Leaderboard containing only system-owned entries (userId = null) and
  My Strategies containing only entries owned by the current authenticated
  user. Each projection must compute its own Top-K, contiguous ranks, and
  updatedAt after scope filtering. Prefer a backward-compatible
  scope=system|mine|combined query on the existing REST endpoint, with combined
  remaining the default for existing clients and the Dashboard. Preserve the
  current Prisma schema, nullable ownership model, global Search Loop, and
  system-safe leaderboard:update invalidation wire. Do not add socket rooms,
  handshakes, namespaces, or client-side authorization filtering.
created: 2026-08-25
